    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d295">

                <pb facs="0346" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/203.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-05T17:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following telegram has been received from Henry, Puerto Plata: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nautilus</hi> has ordered discontinuance
                            artillery by both sides. The situation outwardly same but Bordas
                            probably weakening.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Henry also wires Arias is in Puerto Plata with several hundred soldiers.
                    Reenforcements for Bordas leaving here to-morrow night.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
